meta {
  name: normalize community regions
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{enrichment_url}}/internal/normalize-community-regions
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.scanned: isNumber
  res.body.normalized: isNumber
  res.body.skipped: isNumber
}

docs {
  Nightly lever (the enrichment-refresh CronJob runs it right after
  the catalog refresh trigger), operator-runnable any time: promotes
  free-text community-product regions into the known set, this
  service's twin of collection's normalize-regions, scoped to the
  community products enrichment owns. Exact-or-synonym folding only -
  never fuzzy, so an unreviewed string is left as typed. No fetch arm:
  a community product carries no provider identity to re-fetch, so
  promotion is a plain region field rewrite. Idempotent: a promoted
  row leaves the selection set. Expect 200 with
  scanned/normalized/skipped.

  Guard: admin role or a service token. The bearer behind
  {{access_token}} must be an admin - the folder's dev-token flow logs
  in as alice by default, so run it with body {"user": "admin"} first,
  or override --env-var access_token with a minted admin or service
  token.
}
